1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:02,070
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:03,410
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:05,080
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:05,810 --> 00:00:06,810
(Cheongma Group's Open Competition
for New Designers)

5
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:08,010
(Episode 10)

6
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:15,290
(2026 New Designer Competition:
Application Desk)

7
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:18,460
(Cheongma Group's Open Competition
for New Designers)

8
00:00:23,730 --> 00:00:25,130
So, this is where you are.

9
00:00:26,530 --> 00:00:27,530
Just you wait.

10
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:31,200
I'll find you and make you pay
for what you did.

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,170
(Cheongma Group's Open Competition
for New Designers)

12
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:41,210
Open competition for new designers?

13
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:44,850
(Cheongma Group's Open Competition
for New Designers)

14
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:47,490
(Grand Prize: 50,000 dollars
and a position at Cheongma)

15
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:48,750
The grand prize is...

16
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:52,220
a position in the design office?

17
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:00,600
Well, look who it is.

18
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:11,780
It really is you, Ko Eun Seol.

19
00:01:13,010 --> 00:01:14,350
Oh, right.

20
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:16,680
This is your family's company,
isn't it?

21
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,120
It's been a while.

22
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:20,720
How have you been?

23
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,250
Are you married?

24
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:23,720
No, not yet.

25
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:25,760
Then what about work?

26
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:27,660
I'm looking for a job.

27
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:30,130
I see. You're unemployed.

28
00:01:33,130 --> 00:01:34,330
So what brings you here?

29
00:01:34,630 --> 00:01:36,330
I told you. I'm looking for a job.

30
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,040
I want to work here.

31
00:01:39,570 --> 00:01:41,270
You? At our company?

32
00:01:41,470 --> 00:01:42,470
Why?

33
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:44,140
Is there some reason
I can't work here?

34
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:45,940
Did you even graduate
from high school?

35
00:01:46,510 --> 00:01:47,780
You were expelled.

36
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:51,820
You have a good memory.

37
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:54,550
Or do you remember
because you got me expelled?

38
00:01:54,550 --> 00:01:55,590
Whatever.

39
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:57,590
Let me give you some advice.

40
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,060
Dream on.

41
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:03,430
This isn't a place
someone like you can get into.

42
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:07,400
From what I've learned, Hae Ra,

43
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:10,800
you never know
what's going to happen in life.

44
00:02:12,070 --> 00:02:14,070
So don't be so sure of yourself.

45
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:18,410
I may not know about other things,
but as long as I'm here,

46
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:20,850
you'll never get into Cheongma.

47
00:02:21,510 --> 00:02:22,710
That much is certain.

48
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,620
Why do you hate me so much?

49
00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:29,820
You really don't know?

50
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:32,690
Because you don't know your place.

51
00:02:33,490 --> 00:02:36,390
You were just like this before.
How have you not changed at all?

52
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:41,500
And you're still
as rude and arrogant as ever.

53
00:02:41,570 --> 00:02:42,700
Exactly.

54
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:45,140
Stop getting involved with someone
as rude and arrogant as me,

55
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:46,740
and just go your own way.

56
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:48,940
Don't waste your energy
on a lost cause.

57
00:03:00,290 --> 00:03:01,920
I'm home.

58
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,020
- Hey.
- Hae Ra, hey.

59
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:04,620
Come here for a second.

60
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:07,460
Why?

61
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:09,560
Let me see your phone.

62
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:11,730
Why do you suddenly
want to see my phone?

63
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,930
We're curious what name
you saved us under.

64
00:03:15,330 --> 00:03:16,570
What do you think?

65
00:03:16,970 --> 00:03:18,500
I just have you saved
as Mom and Dad.

66
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:21,470
I knew it.

67
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:24,280
You know, this one young woman
had her dad in her phone...

68
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:27,710
as "My Dearest Dad,"
even with a heart.

69
00:03:29,350 --> 00:03:31,680
Really? What young woman
is that thoughtful?

70
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,590
There was this young woman
I bumped into a few days ago,

71
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:37,090
and we accidentally
swapped our phones.

72
00:03:37,890 --> 00:03:40,360
That's how she had her dad saved
in her contacts.

73
00:03:41,690 --> 00:03:45,360
Her father must've saved
a country in his past life.

74
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:46,700
I'm so jealous.

75
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,670
I know, right?

76
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,670
But when I saw that,

77
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:54,970
it really touched my heart
for some reason.

78
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:59,680
So, Hae Ra,
you should reflect on that.

79
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:02,350
Just "Mom" and "Dad."
That's kind of cold.

80
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:05,020
Well, how do you and Dad
have me saved in your phones?

81
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:06,820
What?

82
00:04:07,890 --> 00:04:08,890
See?

83
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:11,520
The apple doesn't fall far
from the tree.

84
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:19,230
Honey, really. Why start an argument
you know you can't win?

85
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:23,370
I was just jealous of her parents,
that's all.

86
00:04:26,870 --> 00:04:28,140
Do you need something?

87
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:29,910
Ms. Joo.

88
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:32,040
Do you happen to remember
someone named Ko Eun Seol?

89
00:04:33,850 --> 00:04:34,850
Ko Eun Seol?

90
00:04:34,910 --> 00:04:37,650
You know, the girl I got expelled
back in high school.

91
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:40,180
Oh, her.

92
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:42,820
Why are you suddenly
asking about her?

93
00:04:43,290 --> 00:04:44,920
Earlier, I ran into her
in the main lobby.

94
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:46,620
The main lobby?

95
00:04:47,190 --> 00:04:50,090
Can you believe
she wants to work for our company?

96
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:53,930
She said that?

97
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,170
So I told her to keep dreaming.

98
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,600
I said it'll never happen
as long as I'm here.

99
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:06,740
What's on your mind?

100
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,350
Oh, it's nothing.

101
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:13,020
I mean, she was expelled
from high school.

102
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,850
How could she possibly get a job
at our company?

103
00:05:15,150 --> 00:05:17,390
- It's just ridiculous.
- My thoughts exactly.

104
00:05:17,590 --> 00:05:20,020
She still doesn't know her place.

105
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:22,930
This isn't worth eating.

106
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,800
A murderer like her? How could she?

107
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,840
In her dreams.

108
00:05:35,370 --> 00:05:38,440
(Cheongchun Gositel)

109
00:05:48,090 --> 00:05:49,320
(Cheongma Group's Open Competition
for New Designers)

110
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:50,460
(Cheongma's First
Blind Design Contest)

111
00:05:54,990 --> 00:05:56,430
(Cheongma's First
Blind Design Contest)

112
00:05:56,430 --> 00:05:58,300
(Apply)

113
00:06:08,170 --> 00:06:10,240
You're going to enter
the design competition?

114
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:14,210
Yes. But I can't quite do it
on my own.

115
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,780
I'm going to need your help,
Attorney Seo.

116
00:06:17,750 --> 00:06:19,180
What can I do to help?

117
00:06:19,350 --> 00:06:22,390
Well, the competition theme is
"The Rebirth of Cheongma."

118
00:06:23,090 --> 00:06:24,090
And?

119
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:25,790
I need to analyze...

120
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:28,290
all of Cheongma's past collections
and design history,

121
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:31,230
but there's only so much
I can find online.

122
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:33,630
I see.

123
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:36,700
So you're saying you need
Cheongma's internal documents.

124
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:40,100
Yes. Is that possible?

125
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:43,940
But can looking at some documents...

126
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,340
really help you win
the designer competition?

127
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:50,180
Actually, I wanted to go
to art school.

128
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:52,220
I was told I had a real talent.

129
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:55,620
I earned every design certification
while on the inside.

130
00:06:55,950 --> 00:06:57,220
I even had a mentor there.

131
00:06:58,490 --> 00:06:59,720
Who was your mentor?

132
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:01,590
There was a famous designer
in there.

133
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:02,960
She was in for white-collar crime.

134
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:06,800
In that case, it sounds like
it's worth a shot.

135
00:07:07,770 --> 00:07:09,970
All right. I'll see what I can do.

136
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,700
I'm sorry to ask for so much.

137
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,210
Hey, I told you.

138
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:15,570
This isn't just your fight,
Eun Seol.

139
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:30,960
This is a more approachable line...

140
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,860
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

141
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:36,460
Seok Jin. Let's go get lunch.

142
00:07:36,730 --> 00:07:38,000
I ordered in.

143
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,530
Why would you order in?

144
00:07:40,670 --> 00:07:41,870
Let's go eat out together.

145
00:07:42,430 --> 00:07:44,000
I have a mountain of work to do.

146
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:45,740
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

147
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,510
But you don't have to work
through your lunch break.

148
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:51,610
A lot of people are watching me.

149
00:07:52,310 --> 00:07:53,310
Some say I got here via connections,

150
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:54,850
and others say
it's all thanks to them.

151
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:57,280
I have to prove myself
with my skills.

152
00:07:58,350 --> 00:07:59,820
I get the connections part,

153
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,350
but who said
it's all thanks to them?

154
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,120
Someone.

155
00:08:03,550 --> 00:08:04,590
Was it Director Joo?

156
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:08,830
How did you know?

157
00:08:09,730 --> 00:08:10,730
I can't believe her.

158
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:14,700
But it's true you have her to thank.

159
00:08:15,130 --> 00:08:17,940
She pushed out Chief Choi
to get you that position.

160
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:20,440
What?

161
00:08:21,810 --> 00:08:22,810
Anyway,

162
00:08:23,070 --> 00:08:25,710
Director Joo can be scary,
so don't ever make an enemy of her.

163
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:26,980
Got it?

164
00:08:31,850 --> 00:08:33,350
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

165
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:34,590
Is this the Security Team?

166
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:36,290
This is Seo Hyun Jae, head of Legal.

167
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,060
I'm gathering evidence for
a brand IP infringement response.

168
00:08:40,190 --> 00:08:41,890
I need access to the Archive Room,

169
00:08:42,130 --> 00:08:43,530
but my key card isn't working.

170
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,300
The Archive Room has
a high security level,

171
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,770
so it requires
separate authorization.

172
00:08:48,330 --> 00:08:49,870
Who has the authority to approve it?

173
00:08:50,270 --> 00:08:51,340
The Chief of Planning.

174
00:08:52,270 --> 00:08:53,940
As in Chief Cha Seok Jin?

175
00:08:55,270 --> 00:08:57,170
Yes, I understand.

176
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:04,650
A temporary pass
for the Archive Room?

177
00:09:05,950 --> 00:09:09,020
I need to collect evidence for
a brand IP infringement response.

178
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:11,160
This is rather sudden.

179
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:12,920
Has there been an issue
that warrants this?

180
00:09:13,060 --> 00:09:15,260
We've received intelligence about
the overseas counterfeit market.

181
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:17,900
There are reports of a move
to openly copy Cheongma's designs.

182
00:09:18,830 --> 00:09:19,830
Is that so?

183
00:09:21,130 --> 00:09:22,130
All right.

184
00:09:22,330 --> 00:09:25,770
I'll ask Security to issue you
a temporary pass.

185
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:27,640
Thank you.

186
00:09:28,370 --> 00:09:29,670
So you're the head
of the Legal Team.

187
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,080
That's right.

188
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:36,550
We haven't been formally introduced.

189
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:39,480
I'm Cha Seok Jin,
the new Chief of Planning.

190
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:42,520
I'm Seo Hyun Jae.

191
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:45,960
Looks like I'll be working closely
with Legal from now on.

192
00:09:46,490 --> 00:09:47,790
I look forward to working with you.

193
00:09:48,530 --> 00:09:50,230
I look forward to it as well.

194
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:58,070
What's Team Leader Seo
been up to lately?

195
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,970
Why the sudden interest in him?

196
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:04,180
I heard Ko Eun Seol said
she wants to join our company.

197
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:06,780
I'm just wondering...

198
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:09,350
if Mr. Seo might be helping her
in some way.

199
00:10:10,450 --> 00:10:13,250
Sure. I'll look into him.

200
00:10:22,930 --> 00:10:25,000
I sent the temporary pass
by courier.

201
00:10:25,230 --> 00:10:26,230
By courier?

202
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,130
Considering they deleted
the vehicle records,

203
00:10:28,270 --> 00:10:30,400
they probably know I'm helping you.

204
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,770
So I thought it'd be best
to be careful.

205
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:34,940
Right. I see.

206
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,510
Also,

207
00:10:36,710 --> 00:10:38,910
since they also know
what you look like,

208
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:41,410
try to avoid being seen
by the other employees.

209
00:10:42,510 --> 00:10:43,750
Okay, I will.

210
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:47,650
By the way,
how did it go with your brother?

211
00:10:48,290 --> 00:10:49,690
Did you clear up
the misunderstanding?

212
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,360
No.

213
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:55,160
How could a decade-long issue
be resolved so easily?

214
00:10:57,030 --> 00:10:59,430
Anyway, thank you, Attorney Seo.

215
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:02,300
Of course.

216
00:11:17,650 --> 00:11:18,650
I'm home.

217
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,150
Who are you?

218
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:28,560
Hello.
It's been a long time, Mr. Ko.

219
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:30,160
A long time?

220
00:11:30,490 --> 00:11:31,930
Don't you remember him?

221
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:36,070
He's the lawyer who defended
Eun Seol ten years ago.

222
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:39,300
So, what brings you here?

223
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,570
I wanted to talk to you, Eun Guk.

224
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:45,480
I have nothing to say to you.

225
00:11:47,210 --> 00:11:49,750
Do you want your sister
to be the killer?

226
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:54,390
Are you afraid to know you hated
your sister for ten years...

227
00:11:54,450 --> 00:11:55,820
for nothing?

228
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,020
What did you just say?

229
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:04,060
If that's not it,
there's no reason to refuse to talk.

230
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:08,270
Fine. I'll hear you out.

231
00:12:08,670 --> 00:12:09,730
Good, yes.

232
00:12:13,870 --> 00:12:16,410
So, what is it that you want to say?

233
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:20,210
I hear you still think
your sister is guilty.

234
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:23,610
You need to get that straight.
Eun Seol didn't do it.

235
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:27,850
But what about the witness?
There was one, remember?

236
00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:30,150
He committed perjury.

237
00:12:31,690 --> 00:12:32,690
Perjury?

238
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:33,860
That's right.

239
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:37,860
Apparently, the guard took money
and was instructed to lie.

240
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:41,100
Who would instruct him to do that?

241
00:12:41,330 --> 00:12:42,430
The actual killer, I'd imagine.

242
00:12:43,070 --> 00:12:45,300
They must've needed someone
to take the fall for them.

243
00:12:45,370 --> 00:12:47,270
Who was that exactly?

244
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,910
I don't know for sure yet myself.

245
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:55,380
But Eun Seol and I
will definitely find out.

246
00:13:01,820 --> 00:13:03,790
Then why couldn't you
prove it back then?

247
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:05,690
You were Eun Seol's lawyer,
weren't you?

248
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,420
You should've proven it then.

249
00:13:09,430 --> 00:13:10,460
I'm sorry.

250
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:14,300
It was the first case I handled
after becoming a lawyer,

251
00:13:14,730 --> 00:13:16,130
so I was very inexperienced.

252
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:19,470
The witness's testimony
was so powerful,

253
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:21,310
and the trial was rushed through.

254
00:13:22,410 --> 00:13:26,440
That must be why
you're still helping our Eun Seol.

255
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:27,950
Out of guilt.

256
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:31,350
Yes.

257
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:47,830
Don't forget to eat your vegetables.

258
00:13:49,970 --> 00:13:50,970
Uncle.

259
00:13:51,070 --> 00:13:52,540
Are you skipping
breakfast again today?

260
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,170
You eat up, Teun Teun.

261
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:57,240
I'll get going.

262
00:14:00,410 --> 00:14:03,980
Uncle must still be mad at you, Mom.

263
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:14,330
Hyun Jae!

264
00:14:18,030 --> 00:14:19,030
What?

265
00:14:19,630 --> 00:14:21,570
Invite Eun Seol over sometime.

266
00:14:22,870 --> 00:14:24,240
You don't have to force it.

267
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:27,570
I'm not forcing it.
Just ask her when she's free.

268
00:14:29,170 --> 00:14:30,170
Make sure you do.

269
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:47,090
Yes, Eun Guk.

270
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,860
Where is that punk?

271
00:14:50,260 --> 00:14:51,260
Who?

272
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,030
The punk who lied on the stand.

273
00:14:54,670 --> 00:14:56,370
You mean Lee Jung Tae?

274
00:14:56,870 --> 00:14:58,070
Why do you ask?

275
00:14:59,470 --> 00:15:00,470
Where is he?

276
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:05,940
Eun Guk,
Eun Seol and I will handle this,

277
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:07,540
so you stay out of it.

278
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:09,010
Just tell me where he is.

279
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:10,880
Eun Guk, please.

280
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,150
I won't hang up until you tell me.

281
00:15:14,750 --> 00:15:17,290
So just tell me already.
Where is that punk?

282
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:21,830
Attorney Seo!

283
00:15:22,930 --> 00:15:26,860
He's staying at the Yeonju Motel
in Sillim-dong,

284
00:15:27,730 --> 00:15:29,070
but you can't use violence
whatsoever.

285
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:31,270
Do you understand what I'm saying?

286
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:33,840
Hello?

287
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:35,170
Eun Guk?

288
00:15:35,470 --> 00:15:36,540
Eun Guk!

289
00:15:46,450 --> 00:15:49,750
(Baggage Storage)

290
00:16:01,830 --> 00:16:03,770
This is Room 2008
at the Yeonju Motel.

291
00:16:04,030 --> 00:16:06,670
One sweet and sour pork
and two bottles of soju, please.

292
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,320
What the...

293
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,160
Are they kidding me? Darn it!

294
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:39,270
- It's Lee Jung Tae.
- Answer.

295
00:16:42,610 --> 00:16:44,110
Do you have more business with me?

296
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,640
Are you messing with me?

297
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,150
I'm pretty sure I asked
for 100,000 dollars.

298
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,450
You should be grateful
you even got 10,000.

299
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,820
I was going to give you nothing,

300
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,520
but I took pity
on your pathetic life.

301
00:16:55,590 --> 00:16:56,990
So you're calling my bluff?

302
00:16:57,690 --> 00:17:00,290
I could go see Ko Eun Seol
right now, you know.

303
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:06,530
Go ahead.

304
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:07,600
What...

305
00:17:08,330 --> 00:17:09,600
What's making you so confident?

306
00:17:10,330 --> 00:17:12,170
Do you think I won't talk
because I'm an accomplice?

307
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:13,270
You're dead wrong!

308
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:16,770
Your mother is staying
with her sibling in Seosan.

309
00:17:17,510 --> 00:17:18,540
What do you say?

310
00:17:18,810 --> 00:17:20,410
Maybe I'll pay her
a visit right now.

311
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:23,250
What?

312
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:25,780
If you know what's good for you,

313
00:17:25,850 --> 00:17:27,420
get on a plane to Vietnam
and disappear.

314
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:29,420
And don't try any funny business.

315
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:33,660
Good job.

316
00:17:34,630 --> 00:17:35,630
You...

317
00:17:51,410 --> 00:17:52,910
Darn, that was fast.

318
00:18:03,350 --> 00:18:04,420
Lee Jung Tae?

319
00:18:14,060 --> 00:18:16,630
Who are you?
Why are you doing this to me?

320
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:28,780
Which scum told you
to give false testimony?

321
00:18:29,410 --> 00:18:31,110
Who was it? Tell me, now!

322
00:18:31,850 --> 00:18:32,880
What are you talking about?

323
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,150
You don't know?

324
00:18:35,050 --> 00:18:36,450
Then I'll make you understand.

325
00:18:43,190 --> 00:18:45,830
How about that?
Are you starting to get it now?

326
00:18:46,830 --> 00:18:48,100
Tell me. Who was it?

327
00:18:48,170 --> 00:18:51,070
Who told you to frame my sister?

328
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:56,440
Hey. Get back here.

329
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:41,820
(Unregistered Card)

330
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:51,700
(Door Unlocked)

331
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:31,570
(The History Of Cheongma:
50th Anniversary Special Report)

332
00:20:42,050 --> 00:20:43,180
Are you home?

333
00:20:43,510 --> 00:20:47,050
- Yes.
- It's boiling out. Why the hat?

334
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,120
My gosh!

335
00:20:49,050 --> 00:20:50,990
Eun Guk, what happened to your head?

336
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:53,160
It's nothing.

337
00:20:54,090 --> 00:20:55,890
Grandma, why would you
just snatch my hat off?

338
00:20:55,890 --> 00:20:58,260
Gi Han. Come out here!

339
00:20:58,260 --> 00:21:00,760
Eun Guk came home
with his head split open.

340
00:21:01,370 --> 00:21:04,530
What? What do you mean
his head is split open?

341
00:21:04,870 --> 00:21:07,600
What happened?
Did you get in another fight?

342
00:21:09,710 --> 00:21:11,240
Did you get into a fistfight again?

343
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:13,980
This time, it was for a good reason.

344
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:15,810
So don't give me a hard time.

345
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:18,080
What could ever justify
getting into a fistfight?

346
00:21:21,790 --> 00:21:23,650
Wait, hold on.

347
00:21:24,050 --> 00:21:26,720
Are you saying your head got hurt
because of Eun Seol?

348
00:21:26,790 --> 00:21:28,060
It's not because of her.

349
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:30,330
If it's not because of her,
then what is it?

350
00:21:31,530 --> 00:21:32,530
Good for you.

351
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,800
For once, you acted like
a proper big brother.

352
00:21:36,270 --> 00:21:38,840
Your own son came home
with his head split open,

353
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:40,300
and you're praising him for it?

354
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,140
Give me Eun Seol's phone number.

355
00:21:42,210 --> 00:21:43,940
What are you going to say to her?

356
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:45,210
This happened because of her.

357
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:47,140
She should at least pay
his hospital bills.

358
00:21:47,210 --> 00:21:49,510
Come on, just give me her number.

359
00:21:50,410 --> 00:21:51,650
There's no need for that.

360
00:21:54,050 --> 00:21:56,050
This is more than enough
to cover the hospital bills.

361
00:21:57,520 --> 00:21:58,590
What's this?

362
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,700
My gosh, how much is this?

363
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,330
It's 10,000 dollars.

364
00:22:08,870 --> 00:22:10,570
Where did you get this money?

365
00:22:10,870 --> 00:22:12,440
The guy took off, leaving it behind.

366
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:15,310
- What?
- The one who paid him to lie...

367
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:17,110
must've paid him off again.

368
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:18,540
Then this money...

369
00:22:19,310 --> 00:22:20,540
Is it ours now?

370
00:22:23,850 --> 00:22:24,850
No.

371
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:28,020
It's not ours.
It belongs to Eun Seol.

372
00:22:28,050 --> 00:22:30,720
Why give her the money
you got your head busted open for?

373
00:22:30,750 --> 00:22:32,160
Give it here.

374
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:35,490
Because of him,
Eun Seol spent ten years in prison.

375
00:22:36,430 --> 00:22:39,260
This is for her pain and suffering.

376
00:22:40,230 --> 00:22:41,500
Eun Guk!

377
00:22:41,730 --> 00:22:45,470
Then what about all the suffering
I went through because of you?

378
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:50,570
At least that brat
did something right today.

379
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:53,180
What are you talking about?
Gosh, all that money...

380
00:22:54,850 --> 00:22:55,910
The money.

381
00:22:56,710 --> 00:22:59,120
Right.
So how is the competition going?

382
00:23:00,180 --> 00:23:02,350
It's still early,
so we don't have many entries,

383
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:03,820
but the interest is very high.

384
00:23:04,990 --> 00:23:06,620
And how do you know
the interest is high?

385
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:10,290
Daily website visitors
have increased tenfold,

386
00:23:10,460 --> 00:23:12,830
and with hundreds of inquiries
hitting the Q and A board,

387
00:23:12,900 --> 00:23:14,660
we've assigned dedicated staff.

388
00:23:15,270 --> 00:23:17,230
The Cheongma competition is also...

389
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:19,470
consistently trending
in related online communities.

390
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,040
Is that right?

391
00:23:21,910 --> 00:23:23,810
All right. Good work. You may go.

392
00:23:23,810 --> 00:23:24,880
Yes, sir.

393
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:28,850
By the way,

394
00:23:29,810 --> 00:23:31,680
evidence collection
for the brand IP infringement...

395
00:23:31,750 --> 00:23:33,420
will be completed this week.

396
00:23:35,390 --> 00:23:38,390
Evidence collection
for the brand IP infringement?

397
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:40,760
We've been doing that?

398
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:43,160
Wasn't this reported to you, sir?

399
00:23:43,260 --> 00:23:44,900
I just assumed you knew.

400
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:48,130
Who's in charge of that?

401
00:23:48,870 --> 00:23:50,470
The head of the Legal Team
said he was handling it,

402
00:23:50,530 --> 00:23:52,840
so I even issued him
a temporary pass to the Archive.

403
00:23:57,070 --> 00:23:58,710
Tell the head of Legal to come in.

404
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:16,660
Yes, come in.

405
00:24:23,070 --> 00:24:24,270
You called for me, sir?

406
00:24:24,500 --> 00:24:27,240
Word is you're collecting evidence
related to our brand IP.

407
00:24:27,900 --> 00:24:29,110
What's that about?

408
00:24:29,940 --> 00:24:30,940
Oh, that.

409
00:24:31,110 --> 00:24:32,110
We got a tip...

410
00:24:32,110 --> 00:24:34,440
that overseas competitors
are blatantly copying...

411
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:35,580
Cheongma's design patterns.

412
00:24:35,580 --> 00:24:36,650
That's why, sir.

413
00:24:37,650 --> 00:24:40,480
Why wasn't something so important
reported to me?

414
00:24:41,820 --> 00:24:44,390
I was planning to report it
once we had all the evidence.

415
00:24:44,550 --> 00:24:46,120
Right now, it's just a tip,

416
00:24:46,290 --> 00:24:49,430
and I didn't want to confuse you
with inaccurate information.

417
00:24:51,160 --> 00:24:52,800
I'll be the judge of that.

418
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:54,600
From now on,
if anything like this happens,

419
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:56,870
report it to me immediately.
Understood?

420
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,670
Yes, I understand.

421
00:25:11,720 --> 00:25:14,050
- Aren't you going home?
- You go ahead.

422
00:25:15,620 --> 00:25:16,920
Come on.

423
00:25:17,650 --> 00:25:19,190
Are you working late again tonight?

424
00:25:19,820 --> 00:25:22,490
There's no point
in you being in Korea at all.

425
00:25:22,990 --> 00:25:24,230
What do you mean?

426
00:25:24,490 --> 00:25:27,160
We haven't been on
a single proper date yet.

427
00:25:28,330 --> 00:25:30,930
We see each other at work every day.
Why do we need to go on dates?

428
00:25:31,700 --> 00:25:33,640
You told me we needed
to keep things professional at work.

429
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:36,240
After being so strict about that,
now you say we don't need dates?

430
00:25:37,540 --> 00:25:38,540
Did I say that?

431
00:25:39,110 --> 00:25:40,110
Fair enough.

432
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:41,980
But just bear with me
for a little while.

433
00:25:43,510 --> 00:25:46,720
My dad should know
how hard you're working.

434
00:25:47,980 --> 00:25:50,890
He'll acknowledge it
once I show him results.

435
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:52,790
All right.

436
00:25:53,060 --> 00:25:55,530
Since you're trying so hard
to marry me,

437
00:25:55,530 --> 00:25:56,890
I guess I can be patient.

438
00:25:57,230 --> 00:25:58,260
I'm heading out then.

439
00:25:58,660 --> 00:25:59,660
Get home safe.

440
00:26:26,460 --> 00:26:30,060
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

441
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:49,950
I need to collect evidence for
a brand IP infringement response.

442
00:26:50,810 --> 00:26:51,950
This is rather sudden.

443
00:26:52,020 --> 00:26:53,720
Has there been an issue
that warrants this?

444
00:26:53,780 --> 00:26:55,990
We've received intelligence about
the overseas counterfeit market.

445
00:26:56,120 --> 00:26:58,890
There are reports of a move
to openly copy Cheongma's designs.

446
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:01,490
Is that so?

447
00:27:02,630 --> 00:27:03,630
All right.

448
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:07,630
I'll ask Security to issue you
a temporary pass.

449
00:27:07,700 --> 00:27:08,770
By the way,

450
00:27:09,730 --> 00:27:11,570
evidence collection
for the brand IP infringement...

451
00:27:11,570 --> 00:27:13,370
will be completed this week.

452
00:27:15,370 --> 00:27:18,270
Evidence collection
for the brand IP infringement?

453
00:27:19,280 --> 00:27:20,710
We've been doing that?

454
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:23,250
Wasn't this reported to you, sir?

455
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:25,120
I just assumed you knew.

456
00:27:28,180 --> 00:27:33,660
(Chairman's Office)

457
00:28:38,490 --> 00:28:39,590
Who's in there?

458
00:29:01,110 --> 00:29:02,210
Come out. Now.

459
00:29:04,810 --> 00:29:05,920
I said, come out.

460
00:30:29,830 --> 00:30:33,700
(A Trap Called Desire)

461
00:30:33,700 --> 00:30:35,140
I knew this would happen.

462
00:30:35,210 --> 00:30:37,410
This is what you get
for taking in a stranger.

463
00:30:37,770 --> 00:30:38,880
Grandma, what are you doing?

464
00:30:38,980 --> 00:30:39,980
Don't tell me...

465
00:30:40,180 --> 00:30:43,110
Why not let Eun Seol stay
in your annex then?

466
00:30:43,310 --> 00:30:46,020
Do you know
when I first fell for you?

467
00:30:46,120 --> 00:30:47,620
When did you start to like me?

468
00:30:47,780 --> 00:30:49,090
I'm sorry to say this.

469
00:30:49,290 --> 00:30:50,850
I'm afraid that's going to be tough,
Director Joo.

470
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:54,190
What do you think of Chief Cha
as a son-in-law?

471
00:30:54,320 --> 00:30:55,690
What's in it for you?

472
00:30:55,830 --> 00:30:58,160
Just be smart for once, please.

473
00:30:58,230 --> 00:31:00,760
You seem to care more
for Hae Ra than I do.

474
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:02,670
I'm sorry, sir.

475
00:31:03,270 --> 00:31:05,070
I overstepped my bounds, didn't I?

476
00:31:06,140 --> 00:31:08,100
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
